Controlled reclaim of hole-refill backing
========================================

  sudo <userpages4k launcher> ./anon-hole-refill-reclaim --external-reclaim

This separate fixture repeats the concurrent allocation and owner-exit checks
in README.hole-refill-race. It requires the same page ABI, native granule and
visible swap metadata. After the survivor rewrites and verifies its region, it
prints:

  RECLAIM_READY pid=<survivor> base=<hex> bytes=16777216 owner_mm_exited=1

It then waits up to 20 seconds for byte r on stdin. Place only the fixture and
its descendants in a fresh cgroup, with the controller outside that cgroup.
The controller may make at most three writes of "24M swappiness=200" to that
cgroup's memory.reclaim. Leave memory.max/high unchanged and do not reclaim
other cgroups or create global pressure. Bound controller work within the
20-second window.

Record memory.current, memory.swap.current, memory.stat and memory.events, plus
present and valid-swap PTE counts for the reported region. EAGAIN or a partial
reclaim result does not determine success: actual coverage does. Send r after
the bounded attempts, even if coverage is below the required threshold.

Before reading data back, the survivor snapshots pagemap. It requires at least
3072 of 4096 leaves (75%) to contain real swap entries and verifies every byte
after refault. Insufficient coverage fails this qualification rather than
skipping it. Expect three TAP passes, no skips and no unexpected signals or
kernel warnings. Supervisor and child alarms are 35 and 30 seconds; the
fixture's dedicated process group is killed on failure.

MADV_COLD/PAGEOUT compares native folio mapcount with a contiguous PTE batch.
Nonlinear pooled quarters can belong to the same requested region while
occupying separate virtual locations, so those advice operations skip them.
This fixture exercises ordinary cgroup reclaim and nonlinear reverse mapping
without removing the advice path's protection for other mappings.
